OAB - The gut barrier protects the body by blocking harmful substances. When the 
      barrier weakens due to malfunction of aryl hydrocarbon receptor signaling, 
      stabilizing hypoxia-inducible factor can help restore its function. This finding 
      suggests a new strategy to improve gut health in diseases like inflammatory bowel 
      disease.
