TI  - Linking E. coli to fibrosis in Crohn's disease.
PG  - 12-14
LID - S1931-3128(24)00478-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chom.2024.12.011 [doi]
AB  - Intestinal fibrosis associated with Crohn's disease is a serious yet poorly 
      understood clinical complication. In this issue of Cell Host & Microbe, Ahn and 
      colleagues provide evidence that the adherent intestinal E. coli produced the 
      metallophore yersiniabactin, which sequesters zinc to drive intestinal fibrosis 
      in a HIF-1α-dependent manner.
