      beneficial metabolites derived from the microbiota are still poorly understood. 
      Enterobactin (Ent) is a well-known secreted iron-scavenging siderophore made by 
      bacteria to fetch iron from the host or environment. Little was known about the 
      positive role of Ent until a recent discovery in the nematode Caenorhabditis 
      elegans indicated a beneficial role of Ent in promoting mitochondrial iron level 
