TI  - Targeting intratumoral hypoxia to enhance anti-tumor immunity.
PG  - 5-10
LID - S1044-579X(23)00124-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.semcancer.2023.09.002 [doi]
AB  - Cancers express a large battery of genes by which they establish an 
      immunosuppressive tumor microenvironment. Many of these genes are induced by 
      intratumoral hypoxia through transcriptional activation mediated by 
      hypoxia-inducible factors HIF-1 and HIF-2. This review summarizes several recent 
      reports describing hypoxia-induced mechanisms of immune evasion in sarcoma and 
      breast, colorectal, hepatocellular, prostate and uterine cancer. These studies 
      point to several novel therapeutic approaches to improve anti-tumor immunity and 
      increase responses to immunotherapy.
