TI  - FG-4592 alleviates radiation-induced intestinal injury by facilitating recovery 
      of intestinal stem cell and reducing damage of intestinal epithelial.
PG  - 1-10
LID - S0378-4274(21)00917-6 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.toxlet.2021.12.011 [doi]
AB  - Damage of Intestinal Stem Cells (ISCs) is the main cause of radiation 
      induced-intestinal injury (RIII). Recently, hypoxia Inducible factor (HIF) was 
      verified to be critical for promoting proliferation of ISCs, which suggested a 
      protective role of HIF in the RIII. Thus, we investigated the effect of FG-4592, 
      a novel up-regulator of HIF, on the protection of RIII. With/without FG-4592 
      treatment, the abdomen of mice was radiated, and intestinal injury was assessed. 
      Especially, by intestinal organoid culture, the multiplication capacity and 
      differentiation features of ISCs were detected. As a result, FG-4592, a novel 
      up-regulator of HIF could remit RIII and promote regeneration and differentiation 
      of ISCs after radiation, which were depended on HIF-2 rather than HIF-1.
