DP  - 2009 Aug
TI  - Regulation of intestinal iron absorption: the mucosa takes control?
PG  - 84-7
LID - 10.1016/j.cmet.2009.06.009 [doi]
AB  - Two studies (Shah et al., 2009; Mastrogiannaki et al., 2009) show that the 
      hypoxia inducible factor HIF-2alpha is a major player in regulating iron 
      absorption by directly controlling the transcription of iron transporters in the 
      intestine in response to changes in mucosal iron or oxygen levels. The HIF-2alpha 
      mechanism has major effects on iron metabolism which can override the well-known 
      hepcidin-ferroportin regulatory axis.
