TI  - Comparative analysis of family 1 cytochrome p-450 mRNA expression in human 
      intestinal adenocarcinoma and intact portion of the intestine.
PG  - 250-3
AB  - The expression of mRNA of proteins involved in the transformations of cytostatics 
      (cytochrome P-450 1A1 and 1B1 isoforms) and genes encoding proteins participating 
      in their regulation (Ah receptor, AHRR and ARNT) in intestinal tumors and intact 
      portions of the intestine were studied. The expression of cytochrome P-450 1A1 
      increased in poorly differentiated tumors in comparison with its expression in 
      intact portions of the intestine (tumor/intact tissue=1.65). The expression of 
      cytochrome P-450 1B1 was higher in well-differentiated tumors (tumor/intact 
      tissue=1.62). The possibility of practical use of high expression of cytochrome 
      P-450 isoforms in tumors in comparison with intact intestinal tissue is 
      discussed.
